00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:30.960
are what I expect as reasonable parameters."&nbsp;
If you want to for performance reasons, you might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:35.460
have them optional at runtime. But certainly&nbsp;
during unit tests, certainly during integration&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:41.580
test and during your final testing, you want to&nbsp;
have every single routine test to make sure that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:48.420
a state is expecting is actually legit. And in&nbsp;
this case, the one I got wrong, I didn't. 

